    {
      "text": "he drank of the wine, and was drunken, Gen. 9:21. they could not drink of the waters of Marah, Ex. 15:23. Do not drink wine nor strong drink, Lev. 10:9 (Judg. 13:4; Luke 1:15). separate himself from wine and strong drink, Num. 6:3. neither have ye drunk wine or strong drink, Deut. 29:6. one that boweth down upon his knees to drink, Judg. 7:5. I have drunk neither wine nor strong drink, 1 Sam. 1:15. make them drink of the river of thy pleasures, Ps. 36:8. hast made us to drink the wine of astonishment, Ps. 60:3. Wine is a mocker, strong drink is raging, Prov. 20:1. thirsty, give him water to drink, Prov. 25:21 (Rom. 12:20). kings to drink wine; nor for princes strong drink, Prov. 31:4. strong drink unto him that is ready to perish, Prov. 31:6. nothing better for a man, than … eat and drink, Eccl. 2:24. that they may follow strong drink, Isa. 5:11 (2 Ne. 15:11). Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, Isa. 5:22 (2 Ne. 15:22). let us eat and drink; for to morrow, Isa. 22:13 (1 Cor. 15:32). strong drink shall be bitter to them that drink it, Isa. 24:9. We will drink no wine, Jer. 35:6. Thou shalt drink also water by measure, Ezek. 4:11. They drank wine, and praised the gods of gold, Dan. 5:4. drink the wine of the condemned, Amos 2:8. prophesy unto thee of wine and of strong drink, Micah 2:11.",
